  "id": "Compound::DB01126 - Gene::6715",
  "verbalization": "Dutasteride exhibits a strong binding interaction with Srd5a2, which is involved in multiple steroid metabolic pathways, including 3-oxo-5-alpha-steroid 4-dehydrogenase activity, steroid dehydrogenase activity acting on the Ch-ch group of donors, and cholestenone 5-alpha-reductase activity. These pathways are all related to the conversion of steroid molecules, and Srd5a1 is a known participant in these processes. The evidence suggests that Dutasteride may influence Srd5a1 through its interaction with Srd5a2, potentially modulating the activity of Srd5a1 in steroid metabolism. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The overlapping roles of Srd5a2 and Srd5a1 in steroid metabolism suggest that Dutasteride could act as a modulator of Srd5a1 function, possibly through a shared pathway or regulatory mechanism.",
